column323:
07/Nov/23 11:11 AM;62fb91b70bb03d8a6cb27d59;{quote}Where to store files in asp{quote}

There is a default content root path. You can get it by injecting {{IHostEnvironment _env;}}` and then calling the property {{_env.ContentRootPath}}`;

{quote}What folder structure to use, so that we can store files per Product (do we dump all files in one folder and just access them by filename or do we store all product files in separated folders{quote}

We can choose any structure, because there is an easy way to generate unique file name by adding guid to the file name by using static function {{Guid.NewGuid().ToString()}}`. My personal preference is to create separate folder for each product and name the folder by product id or product number, both of those are generated by sequencer in db and should be unique. Product id probably will be easier, because you have to pass the product id with the upload anyway to use it as a FK for the file table in the db. 

{quote}Later on we need to be able to download each file separately but also all files of one product together as zip file{quote}

This is another reason to use a folder structure. This way on multiple files download we can avoid requesting db for all the filenames for the product and just get the folder with productId/ProductNumber

{quote}How to start the upload and how to recognize the upload being finished.{quote}

[Asp.net|http://Asp.net] Zero uses upload library on the frontend [ng2-file-upload|https://valor-software.com/ng2-file-upload/] . This library provides {{FileUploader}} class that can manage the upload. It also allows multiple files upload with queue management and a {{progress}} property to check on the upload progress. In addition it provides function that return a response after the file upload is finished. There is also an automatic upload functionality and a drag&drop functionality

{quote}  What kind of information does the Upload Field Component need to provide (just a file path? Something else, just an event etc.){quote}

{{FileUploader}} class uses {{FIleItem}} class for upload, that  accepts standard TS {{File}} object and formdata for additional properties you need to pass.  

{quote}In general think about a way on how to process the upload via this component when integrated in the hsu-client.{quote}

Since the {{ng2-file-upload}} library provides all the needed functionality our upload component can be a simple div with styling. Or we can implement the drug&drop functionality and return the {{File}} object and use it with the {{FileUploader}} class.  



[https://pmsoftware.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/HSU/pages/3793813511/File+upload|https://pmsoftware.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/HSU/pages/3793813511/File+upload|smart-link]  - Confluence page with basic examples.

