This Ticket is about to setup the multi-language feature in our own client.

Therefore we need to install the {{abp-ng2-module}}. And try to reverse engineer all services in the frontend making this feature work in the default client. You can start by having a look at {{client/src/shared/common/pipes/localize.pipe.ts}}

The default language should be german. You can find all translation files in: {{backend/src/PMHelmutSchmidtPortal.Core/Localization/PMHelmutSchmidtPortal}}. Notice: the file without language suffix is the default one for asp and is in english. So you probably have to set the default language in some angular.config file (have a look at the default client for that as well).

